From: LineageOS for PCs
Subject: [PATCH] kmod: load modules with a static helper while modprobe_path is empty

With CONFIG_STATIC_USERMODEHELPER every request runs the one fixed helper and
modprobe_path is only its argv[0]. Android's init clears modprobe_path in
early-init and the device gives it back afterwards, while ueventd already
loads drivers: one that asks for a module by name in between (HD Audio for its
codec driver, iwlwifi for iwlmvm) loses the request and gives up. The helper
decides what loads (device/pc/pc_x86_64/rootdir/pc-modprobe.sh).
---
diff --git a/kernel/module/kmod.c b/kernel/module/kmod.c
index a25dccdf7..eea3b8afe 100644
--- a/kernel/module/kmod.c
+++ b/kernel/module/kmod.c
@@ -143,7 +143,11 @@ int __request_module(bool wait, const char *fmt, ...)
 	 */
 	WARN_ON_ONCE(wait && current_is_async());
 
-	if (!modprobe_path[0])
+	/*
+	 * With one fixed helper the path is only argv[0]: Android's init clears it at boot and gives it back
+	 * later, and a driver probing in between (ueventd loads them meanwhile) would lose its request.
+	 */
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_STATIC_USERMODEHELPER) && !modprobe_path[0])
 		return -ENOENT;
 
 	va_start(args, fmt);
